	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"&9&lPowah.&r The straightforward power mod - and the one you should lean on while you fight with everything else."
				""
				"No gases to plumb, no heat to manage, no meltdowns. Powah scales by &ltier&r rather than by complexity: seven rungs from Starter to Nitro, and every machine in the mod climbs the same ladder."
				""
				"&7Burn solids, burn lava, catch sunlight, then split uraninite. Buffer it in cells, move it in cables, and finally throw it across the solar system with Ender Cells that need no wire at all.&r"
				""
				"&8Uraninite does not spawn in the void - the SkyForge keystone bridges you a starter supply, and Mystical Agriculture seeds make it sustainable."
			]
			icon: "powah:energizing_orb"
			id: "7B00000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000001"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Seven tiers, no meltdowns"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000001"
				title: "Begin Powah"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&9Powah"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 2.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000001"]
			description: [
				"The keystone bridge turns Sky Dust into &eUraninite&r - Powah's reactor fuel, and an ore that will never spawn in the void. Bank a few; the reactor eats them."
				""
				"&e&lThis is a bridge recipe, not a real supply.&r SkyForge exists to break chicken-and-egg problems: Powah needs uraninite, uraninite needs an overworld, and you do not have one. The keystone gets you started - it does not scale."
				""
				"&e&lThe scalable answer is Mystical Agriculture.&r Uraninite seeds turn reactor fuel into a crop you harvest. If you intend to run reactors seriously - and this chapter assumes you will - get that farm going early rather than bridging one ingot at a time."
				""
				"&e&lWhat it feeds:&r Powah's &7Uraninite &8→&7 Uranium&r line, and from there the Reactor tiers that carry your grid from First Machines to the fission plant in Ascension."
				""
				"&7Powah reactors consume fuel continuously while running, unlike the Thermo and Wind generators you have been leaning on. Budget for a steady supply before you commit your base to one.&r"
				""
				"&8The same keystone bridges osmium for Mekanism and certus for AE2. One block, three tech trees unlocked."
			]
			icon: "powah:uraninite"
			id: "2103000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2103000000000102"
				item: "powah:uraninite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Reactor fuel from nothing"
			tasks: [{
				count: 4L
				id: "2103000000000202"
				item: "powah:uraninite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Bridged Uranium"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000002"]
			description: [
				"The &eEnergizing Orb&r crafts Powah's tiered materials - toss items into the field, feed it power, get the next tier out."
				""
				"Every Powah machine climbs the same ladder: &7Basic &8→ &7Hardened &8→ &7Blazing &8→ &7Niotic &8→ &7Spirited &8→ &7Nitro&r. This is where you build up it."
			]
			icon: "powah:energizing_orb"
			id: "2103000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000103"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Craft the tiered materials"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000203"
				item: "powah:energizing_orb"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Energizing Orb"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000003"]
			description: [
				"A &eThermo Generator&r sat over lava makes passive FE forever, no fuel runs required. Drop a few and stop thinking about power for a while."
				""
				"&e&lIt runs on a temperature difference, not on burning fuel.&r Lava on one side, cooler air or water on the other, and it produces indefinitely. The lava is &lnot consumed&r - one bucket powers it forever."
				""
				"&e&lWhich makes it perfect here.&r You already have a lava source for your cobble generator, and SkyForge gives you lava synthesis. Free heat you were making anyway."
				""
				"&7Surround it with water or place it in a cold biome to widen the temperature gap - output goes up. A generator sitting in the Nether next to lava produces almost nothing, because everything around it is already hot.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt is slow but utterly reliable&r - no fuel logistics, no moving parts, no maintenance. Build a bank of them as your baseline grid and let the reactors handle peaks."
				""
				"&8Between this and wind, you can run all of First Machines without ever crafting a fuel-burning generator."
			]
			icon: "powah:thermo_generator_basic"
			id: "2103000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "2103000000000104"
				item: "minecraft:blaze_rod"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Passive power over lava"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000204"
				item: "powah:thermo_generator_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Free Heat"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2103000000000004"]
			description: [
				"The &ePowah Reactor&r is a 36-block multiblock that burns your bridged Uraninite for serious, sustained FE."
				""
				"This is the power plant that carries you through the tech branches, off-world, and eventually into Mekanism fission. Build the whole thing."
			]
			icon: "powah:reactor_basic"
			id: "2103000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				count: 32
				id: "2103000000000107"
				item: "powah:uraninite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "&7The power plant"
			tasks: [{
				count: 36L
				id: "2103000000000207"
				item: "powah:reactor_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Going Nuclear"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&eCapacitors&r are the component every Powah machine is built around - generators, cells, cables, reactors, all of them."
				""
				"&e&lThey come in the same tier ladder as everything else in Powah:&r &7Starter &8→ &7Basic &8→ &7Hardened &8→ &7Blazing &8→ &7Niotic &8→ &7Spirited &8→ &7Nitro&r."
				""
				"&e&lThere are also Tiny and Large variants&r at each tier. Recipes are specific about which they want - check JEI rather than assuming a Large will substitute for a plain one."
				""
				"&7Every tier upgrade in this chapter means crafting a batch of the next capacitor first. Build them in bulk; you will never regret having spares.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:capacitor_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000002"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The component in everything"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000200"
				item: "powah:capacitor_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Capacitors"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000002"]
			description: [
				"&eDielectric Paste&r, &eRods&r and &eCasing&r are Powah's structural materials - the housing that every machine and reactor is wrapped in."
				""
				"&e&lPaste is the base&r, made from blaze powder, clay and ender pearls. Rods and casing are pressed from it."
				""
				"&c&lThis is the quiet bottleneck of the whole mod.&r Reactors in particular eat casing by the stack. If you intend to run the nuclear line, set up a bulk paste supply before you start rather than crafting it nine at a time."
				""
				"&7Ender pearls in a void world mean either an Enderman farm or Mystical Agriculture seeds. Plan for it.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:dielectric_casing"
			id: "7B00000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000003"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Paste, rods and casing"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7B02000000000300"
					item: "powah:dielectric_paste"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7B02000000000301"
					item: "powah:dielectric_casing"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Dielectric Materials"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000002"]
			description: [
				"&eEnergy Cables&r move Forge Energy between Powah machines and anything else that accepts FE."
				""
				"&e&lThey are tiered like everything here&r, and the tier sets throughput. A Basic cable running from a Nitro Reactor will waste most of what the reactor makes."
				""
				"&7They interoperate with Mekanism Universal Cables and every other FE system in the pack - use whichever you have most of. There is no advantage to keeping the networks separate.&r"
				""
				"&8If a machine seems starved, check cable tier before adding generators. This catches people in every FE mod."
			]
			icon: "powah:energy_cable_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000004"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Powah's own wiring"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000400"
				item: "powah:energy_cable_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Energy Cables"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000004"]
			description: [
				"&eEnergy Cells&r store FE. Same seven tiers, each holding dramatically more than the last."
				""
				"&e&lThey are the correct thing to put between a reactor and your base.&r Reactor output is steady; your base's demand is spiky. The cell absorbs the difference and stops machines browning out when several start at once."
				""
				"&e&lCells have a configurable output side&r - set it with a wrench so the cell pushes into your network rather than sitting full."
				""
				"&7A charged cell is also portable power. Carry one to a new build site rather than running cable across the island for a job that takes ten minutes.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:energy_cell_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000005"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Buffer the peaks"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000500"
				item: "powah:energy_cell_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Energy Cells"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000005"]
			description: [
				"The &eFurnator&r burns solid fuel - coal, charcoal, wood, anything a furnace accepts - and produces FE."
				""
				"&e&lThis is Powah's simplest generator and the right first one.&r You already have infinite wood from saplings and a Crook, which makes charcoal effectively free."
				""
				"&7Feed it from a Logistical Transporter or a hopper off your charcoal supply and it runs unattended.&r"
				""
				"&8It will not carry a late-game base, but it will comfortably run your first machine room while you build toward reactors."
			]
			icon: "powah:furnator_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000006"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Burn solids for power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000600"
				item: "powah:furnator_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Furnator"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000006"]
			description: [
				"The &eMagmator&r burns lava for FE - considerably more energy-dense than solid fuel."
				""
				"&e&lThis is where your Cyclic Melter earns its keep.&r Cobble into the Melter, lava out, lava into the Magmator, power out. Cobblestone is infinite, so this is a closed loop that runs on nothing."
				""
				"&7Pipe lava in with Mechanical Pipes and buffer it in a tank - a Magmator fed directly from a Melter stalls whenever the Melter pauses.&r"
				""
				"&8Unlike Mekanism's Thermo Generator, the Magmator CONSUMES the lava. It is faster, but it is not free."
			]
			icon: "powah:magmator_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000007"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Lava straight into FE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000700"
				item: "powah:magmator_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Magmator"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000007"]
			description: [
				"&ePowah Solar Panels&r generate FE in daylight, across the same seven-tier ladder."
				""
				"&e&lA void island is close to the ideal site&r - no terrain shadow, no caves, nothing above you. Roof your base in panels and they run at full output all day."
				""
				"&c&lThey stop at night&r, so pair them with an Energy Cell sized to carry your base through darkness, or run them alongside a Furnator that picks up the slack."
				""
				"&7Higher tiers are dramatically better rather than incrementally - it is usually worth upgrading a small array rather than expanding a low-tier one.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:solar_panel_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000008"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Daylight, tiered"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000800"
				item: "powah:solar_panel_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Powah Solar Panels"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000008"]
			description: [
				"&eEnergizing Rods&r are what actually deliver power to the Energizing Orb. The Orb is only the crafting surface; the rods are the machine."
				""
				"&e&lMore rods, and higher tier rods, mean faster crafts.&r A single Basic rod will technically complete a recipe eventually. Six Nitro rods will do it before you have walked away."
				""
				"&e&lPlace them around the Orb&r with a clear line to it, and feed them with cable. The Orb's GUI shows total input rate - use it to check whether adding rods is actually helping."
				""
				"&7Late Powah recipes want enormous energy per craft. This is where an Energy Cell bank pays off, discharging into the rods far faster than your generators could directly.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:energizing_rod_basic"
			id: "7B00000000000009"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B01000000000009"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Feeding the Orb"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000900"
				item: "powah:energizing_rod_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Energizing Rods"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B00000000000009"]
			description: [
				"Powah's &eReactor&r is a multiblock that consumes uraninite and produces FE continuously - the backbone of a serious base."
				""
				"&e&lThe build is a solid cube of reactor blocks&r with a controller. Bigger tiers mean bigger cubes and far more output."
				""
				"&e&lIt needs coolant.&r Feed it water, or better, a coolant fluid. An overheating reactor throttles itself down to nothing - it will not explode like Mekanism fission, but it will quietly stop paying you."
				""
				"&c&lFuel is consumed continuously&r, unlike your Thermo Generators. Get Mystical Agriculture uraninite seeds running before you commit the base to reactor power, or you will be babysitting fuel forever."
				""
				"&7Output scales hard with tier. A Nitro reactor makes a Basic one look like a decoration.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:reactor_basic"
			id: "7B0000000000000A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B0100000000000A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Uraninite into serious power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000A00"
				item: "powah:reactor_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Reactor Tiers"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0000000000000A"]
			description: [
				"&eEnder Cells&r transfer energy wirelessly between linked cells - no cable, any distance, across dimensions."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the reason to care about Powah beyond generation.&r One cell at your reactor bank, another on the Moon, and your off-world base is powered from home. No Quantum Ring required."
				""
				"&e&lLink them with a &fBinding Card&r&e:&r right-click the source cell to bind the card, then right-click the destination. The &7dimensional&r binding card variant is what makes cross-planet links work."
				""
				"&7Tier sets transfer rate. A Basic ender cell will trickle; a Nitro one will run a full off-world machine room.&r"
				""
				"&8Between this and the Mekanism Entangloporter you never need to lay cable between islands again."
			]
			icon: "powah:ender_cell_basic"
			id: "7B0000000000000B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B0100000000000B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Wireless energy, any distance"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000B00"
				item: "powah:ender_cell_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Ender Cells"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0000000000000B"]
			description: [
				"An &eEnder Gate&r is a hub that several Ender Cells can bind to, so you can distribute from one source to many destinations without pairing every cell individually."
				""
				"&e&lThe practical setup:&r gate at your main power bank, cells at each outpost bound to the gate. Add an outpost later and you bind one card rather than rewiring anything."
				""
				"&7It also lets you keep a single point of control - unbind the gate and every outpost drops at once, which is occasionally exactly what you want.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:ender_gate_basic"
			id: "7B0000000000000C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B0100000000000C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Many cells, one hub"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000C00"
				item: "powah:ender_gate_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Ender Gates"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0000000000000B"]
			description: [
				"The &ePlayer Transmitter&r beams energy directly into whatever you are carrying - jetpacks, Free Runners, a Meka-Tool, a Draconic pickaxe."
				""
				"&e&lBind it to yourself with a Binding Card&r and it keeps your gear topped up while you are in range. With a dimensional card, from anywhere."
				""
				"&c&lThis quietly solves the single most annoying failure mode in the pack&r - Free Runners going flat mid-fall, a jetpack cutting out over the void, a MekaSuit module dying when you need it."
				""
				"&7Feed it from an Energy Cell. It draws steadily rather than in bursts.&r"
			]
			icon: "powah:player_transmitter"
			id: "7B0000000000000D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B0100000000000D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Charge yourself, wirelessly"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000D00"
				item: "powah:player_transmitter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Player Transmitter"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0000000000000D"]
			description: [
				"&eBatteries&r are portable FE storage - charge one at base, carry it, use it to top up tools and machines in the field."
				""
				"&e&lUseful specifically for building off-world&r, where you arrive with no grid and need to run an Oxygen Distributor immediately. A charged Nitro battery will hold a small outpost over until you get generation up."
				""
				"&7They charge from any FE source and will charge items in your inventory automatically.&r"
				""
				"&8Cheaper and more flexible than carrying an Energy Cell block, though it holds far less."
			]
			icon: "powah:battery_basic"
			id: "7B0000000000000E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B0100000000000E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Power in your pocket"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B02000000000E00"
				item: "powah:battery_basic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Portable Batteries"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0000000000000C"]
			description: [
				"The &eLens of Ender&r lets you see ore and blocks through terrain in a radius around you."
				""
				"&e&lPractically useless at home&r - your island is hollow. Genuinely good on the Moon, Mars, Venus, Glacio and in the Aether, where there is real stone hiding real ore."
				""
				"&7Pair it with the Mekanism Digital Miner: lens to find out whether a spot is worth mining, miner to strip it without digging.&r"
				""
				"&8Costs energy while active. Keep it charged or it simply does nothing."
			]
